Open Vanilla 0021: Duels, quick 1v1 matches on a realm of their own (hetzner/duels_up.sh).

A Warfront world server with OpenVanilla.Duels = 1 (and OpenVanilla.Warfront = 1, for the kits, the gear
picker and the arena) runs Duels:
- A new arena mode, u1: an unrated practice 1v1 (players from one network address may meet; rated play
  still never pits an address against itself). Added last, so every existing mode keeps its number and the
  live line keeps its order; the u1 count goes at the end of it.
- 1v1 matches (d1, u1) are best of OpenVanilla.Duels.Rounds (3). OpenVanilla.Duels.PrepSeconds (15) before
  the first round, OpenVanilla.Duels.RoundPrepSeconds (5) between rounds, OpenVanilla.Duels.RoundMinutes (5)
  per round (then more health wins the round). Between rounds both players go back to their gates, are
  revived and healed, lose the last round's effects and cooldowns, and see "round,<n>,<mine>,<theirs>".
  Drawn rounds are replayed (at most twice the best-of in all). Leaving ends the match as a loss, as before.
  The result line gets ",<mine>-<theirs>" at the end.
- Every finished match goes to warfront_arena_result (realm/duels/duels_characters.sql): mode, time, length,
  winner, rounds, both sides (name:class:guid) and the rating change; the website's ladder and feed come
  from it (duels_up.sh live).
- "hi" answers with a sixth field: 1 on a Duels realm, so the Duels addon shows itself.
The rules for rounds are pure functions in OpenVanilla/DuelsLogic.h (tests: realm/duels/tests).
Off unless OpenVanilla.Duels = 1: Warfront itself behaves as before, apart from the extra live field and the
extra "hi" field, which its addon ignores.

diff --git a/src/game/OpenVanilla/DuelsLogic.h b/src/game/OpenVanilla/DuelsLogic.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7f07dd9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/game/OpenVanilla/DuelsLogic.h
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+/*
+ * Open Vanilla — Duels' pure rules (GPLv2, as CMaNGOS): rounds of a best-of 1v1 match. No game
+ * objects, so realm/duels/tests/test_rounds.cpp runs them without a server. Used by WarfrontArena.cpp.
+ */
+
+#ifndef OPENVANILLA_DUELS_LOGIC_H
+#define OPENVANILLA_DUELS_LOGIC_H
+
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <cstdint>
+
+namespace Warfront
+{
+    namespace Arena
+    {
+        // "Best of" from a setting: odd, 1..7 (an even number goes up by one).
+        inline uint32_t RoundsBestOf(uint32_t setting)
+        {
+            uint32_t n = std::max<uint32_t>(1, std::min<uint32_t>(setting, 7));
+            return n % 2 ? n : n + 1;
+        }
+
+        // After `played` rounds with these scores in a best of `bestOf`: the winning team (0 or 1),
+        // or -1 while the match goes on. Drawn rounds (both dead, or even health at the time limit)
+        // are replayed, up to 2 x bestOf rounds in all; then the higher score wins, or 2 for a draw.
+        inline int RoundOutcome(uint32_t score0, uint32_t score1, uint32_t bestOf, uint32_t played)
+        {
+            uint32_t need = bestOf / 2 + 1;
+            if (score0 >= need)
+                return 0;
+            if (score1 >= need)
+                return 1;
+            if (played >= 2 * bestOf)
+                return score0 > score1 ? 0 : (score1 > score0 ? 1 : 2);
+            return -1;
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+#endif
